# This directory is a Linux container build context, and the repo is developed
# on Windows with core.autocrlf=true — so a plain checkout would hand
# `docker build` a CRLF Dockerfile whose `RUN set -eux; \` continuations carry a
# trailing carriage return into the shell.
#
# Nothing is COPY'd into the image here, so this cannot produce `dev-base/`'s
# shebang failure — but the reason to pin it is the same one, and pinning is
# free. CI never sees the difference (Linux checkouts are LF either way); a
# developer building the image on their own machine does.
* text eol=lf
